.TITLE "ps"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Reports a snapshot of current processes. It displays information about __active programs__ including their process ID, terminal, and execution time.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**ps**
Displays processes associated with the current terminal session.
> 

**ps -A**
Lists all currently running processes on the system.
> __-A__ all processes flag

**ps -u user**
Displays processes owned by a specific user.
> __-u__ user flag | __user__ target username

**ps -e -f**
Shows a full-format listing of every process running on the system.
> __-e__ every process flag | __-f__ full format flag

**ps -m**
Displays the threads associated with each process.
> __-m__ threads flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The BSD version of __ps__ on macOS uses different flags than the GNU version found on Linux. For example, __ps -A__ is the standard way to see all processes, whereas Linux users often use __ps -e__.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:top** **mac:kill**

